lines=['# Fifty-patch blinded Sol review — 16 November 2026','','Completed **50 additional patch reviews**, excluding every patch ID in the earlier ten-patch pilot. Three fresh `gpt-6-sol` workers used low reasoning effort, reviewing 17/17/16 cases with five actual image inspections per case (**250 images**).','','## Blinding and selection','','Reviewers received only anonymous case IDs, copied PNGs, source-free image settings and a common visual protocol. Original patch IDs, coordinates/world files, registry identifiers, previous results and the evaluator key were withheld. They were not told which images contained known records. PNG chunks were checked for location/text metadata. Input hashes and the evaluator-key commitment were recorded. No named-site/CNS leakage was found in output text. File-access restriction was procedural, not a separate OS sandbox.','','The evaluator selected eight new crops containing public reference points across five mapped records, plus 32 high-support, six intermediate-support and four boundary crops without a mapped reference point inside the square. Other crop centres were separated by at least 300 m; reference crops can overlap one another and terrain in the earlier pilot. This is not a random parish survey, and reference-free crops are not verified archaeological negatives.','','## Results','','Follow-up priorities: **'+', '.join(f'{v} {k}'for k,v in summary['followUpCounts'].items())+'**. '+str(summary['casesWithCandidateFlags'])+' cases contain at least one tentative localized feature flag; '+str(summary['candidateCount'])+' candidate annotations were recorded in total.','','A candidate centre was within 25 m of a public reference point in **'+str(summary['referenceCropsWithAnyCentreNear25m'])+'/8 reference crops**; with the predeclared localized-box filter, **'+str(summary['referenceCropsWithLocalizedCentreNear25m'])+'/8**. These proximity results span **'+str(summary['recordsWithLocalizedCentreNear25m'])+'/5 distinct inventory records** under that filter. They are **not archaeological detection rates**.','','The comparison criteria were fixed while reviews were running, before the coordinator read their observations: centre within 50 pixels (25 m), and for a localized flag, box area at most 16,000 pixels (10% of the image) with maximum side 200 pixels (100 m). The threshold is exploratory, not an inventory accuracy tolerance or a surveyed footprint. A point-in-crop does not guarantee a visible structure; buried, removed, diffuse or mislocated features cannot be scored as visible positives. Broad cultivation or rock flags near a point do not establish archaeological recognition.','','| Case | Patch | Reference CNS | Follow-up | Nearest candidate centre | Localized flag within 25 m |','| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
